    "chunk_text": "(4) Any property, right or thing vested, belonging,dedicated or associated with the Spiritual Head orAssociation from and after the date of commencement ofthis Act, shall be vested with the Corporation.\n\n3.The general objects of the Corporation are herebydeclared to be\u2014\n\n(b)to appoint, remove and exercise control over trusteesappointed to the list of institutions set out in theFirst Schedule to this Act;\n\n(c)to administer and supervise all Mosques, Thakkiyas,Madrasas, Charitable Trusts, Muslim Shrines andPlaces of Religious resort and other institutions that\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n30\n\n3Thareeqathul Aroosiyyathil QaadhiriyyahAssociation of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nmay be owned, possessed, dedicated, associated oraffiliated to the Corporation including theappointment, removal and exercise of control overtrustees appointed over the said Mosques,Thakkiyas, Madrasas, Charitable Trusts, MuslimShrines and Places of Religious resort;\n\n(d)to institute legal proceedings to recover anyproperty or sue in action vested, belonging,dedicated or associated with the Spiritual Head ofthe Association;\n\n(e)to institute legal proceedings to advance any of theobjects of the Association;\n\n(f)to conduct religious and spiritual rites of theAssociation;\n\n(g)to promote the sunnath wal jamaath way of Islamiclife which is the mazhab oriented ThareeqathulAroosiyyathil Qaadhiriyyah sufistic instruction ofthe Founder Shaikh among the adherents of theIslamic faith;\n\n(h)to disseminate the mazhab oriented doctrines andteachings of Islam, Islamic culture and Sufism andthe promotion of activities for the benefit of thecommunity;\n\n(i)to conduct research on the work and life of theFounder Shaikh;\n\n(j)to construct and manage Mosques, Thakkiyas,Madrasas, Charitable Trusts, Muslim Shrines andPlaces of Religious resort and other institutions;\n\n(k)to collect funds and accept endowments andmaterials for the building, repair or maintenance ofMosques, Thakkiyas, Madrasas, Charitable Trusts,30"
