    "chunk_text": "(j)to construct and manage Mosques, Thakkiyas,Madrasas, Charitable Trusts, Muslim Shrines andPlaces of Religious resort and other institutions;\n\n(k)to collect funds and accept endowments andmaterials for the building, repair or maintenance ofMosques, Thakkiyas, Madrasas, Charitable Trusts,30\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nMuslim Shrines and Places of Religious resort andother institutions and the conduct of religious andspiritual rites;\n\n(l)to alleviate poverty;\n\n(m)for the advancement of education;\n\n(n)to administer and manage properties of theAssociation;\n\n(o)to do all such other acts and things as are necessary,ancillary or incidental to the attainment of all orany of the objects of the Corporation.\n\n4.(1) The Corporation shall have the power to do,perform and execute all such acts, matters and thingswhatsoever as are necessary or desirable for the promotionor furtherance of the objects of the Corporation or any oneof them including the power to open, operate or close non-interest bearing bank accounts, to borrow or raise moneyfree of interest with or without security, to receive, collect,disburse grants and donations, to invest its funds to constructany buildings on any land vested in, or acquired or held bythe Corporation, to acquire, purchase, lease or rent land, toinvest in movable property and chooses in action, and toengage, employ and dismiss personnel for the purpose ofcarrying out all or any of the objects of the Corporation:\n\nProvided, however, the powers of the Corporation shallat all times be exercised in compliance with the principlesof sunnath wal jamaath.\n\n(2) The Corporation shall also have the power to institutelegal proceedings in respect of any property claimed to beowned, possessed, belonging to , dedicated or associatedwith or managed for and on behalf of the Founding SpiritualHead, Association or Corporation as the case may be.30\n\nGeneralPowers of theCorporation.\n\n5Thareeqathul Aroosiyyathil QaadhiriyyahAssociation of Sri Lanka (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25"
