    "chunk_text": "(i) to do all such other acts and things as are necessaryfor and incidental or conducive to the attainment allor any of the objects.\n\n(2) In the implementation of the objects specified insubsection (1) the Corporation shall ensure that such\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nGreat Wall of Nibbana DevelopmentFoundation (Incorporation)3\n\nimplementation shall be carried out without any discriminationbased on race, religion, language, caste, sex, ploitical opinion,place of birth or any of such gounds.\n\n4.The objects of the Corporation shall be carried out insuch manner so as not to create any conflict between the workof the Corporation and any work being carried outsimultaneously by any Minister or Department of theGovernment or any Provincial Council.\n\n5.(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act the Corporationshall be carried out by a Board of Directors (hereinafterreferred to as\u201cthe Board\u201d, consisiting of such number ofoffice bearers as may be specified by the rules made undersection 7.\n\n(2)(a) The Board of Directors of the foundation that holdsoffice on the day immediately preceding the date ofcommencement of this Act, shall function as the Board of theCorporation until the first Board is appointed or elected inthe manner provided for by rules made under section 7.\n\n(b) The first Board of the Corporation shall be appointedor elected within one year of the date of commencement ofthis Act.\n\n(3)(a) Every office bearer of the Board including thepatrons and advisers, shall be appointed or elected for a periodof three years and any such office bearer, patron or advisorshall be eligible for re-appointment or re-election after lapseof the said period of three years.\n\n(b) In the event of a vacancy occurring due to the death,resignation, incapacity or removal from office of an officebearer, the Board shall having regard to the rules of theCorporation, elect or appoint a person to fill such vacancy.\n\nCorporation toensure noconflict withwork ofMinistry orDepartment ofthe CentralGovernment orProvince."
