    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 164]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice on 21st February, 2017\n\n(Published in the Gazette on January 23, 2017)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n2-2d\n\n2-\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nREVOCATION OF IRREVOCABLE DEEDS OF GIFTON THE GROUND OF GROSS INGRATITUDE\n\nto provide for the revocation of Irrevocable Deeds of Gift on the groundof Gross Ingratitude and for matters connected therewith and incidentalthereto.\n\n2\u2014PL 005046\u2014475 (02/2017)\n\n1 Revocation of Irrevocable Deeds of Gifton the ground of Gross Ingratitude\n\n2\u2014PL 004957\u2014 475 (12/2016)\n\nShort title.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 53/2015.\n\nAN ACT TO PROVIDE FOR REVOCATION OF IRREVOCABLE DEEDS OF GIFT\n\nON THE GROUND OF GROSS INGRATITUDE AND FOR MATTERS CONNECTED\n\nTHEREWITH AND INCIDENTAL THERETO\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Revocation ofIrrevocable Deeds of Gift on the ground of Gross IngratitudeAct, No. of 2017.\n\n2.An irrevocable deed of gift may be revoked onthe ground of gross ingratitude, only on an Order madeby a competent court, in an action filed by the donorof such deed against the donee to have the saiddeed revoked.\n\n3.Court shall not entertain an action referred toin section 2, unless it is filed within a period of ten yearsfrom the date of the execution of such deed of gift andwithin two years from the date on which the cause ofaction arose.\n\n4.(1) The plaintiff in an action instituted under theprovisions of this Act shall file or cause to be filed in courtwith the plaint, an application for registration of lispendens\u2014\n\n(a)addressed to the Registrar of Lands of the district inwhich the deed which is sought to be revoked isregistered; or"
