    "chunk_text": "(p) to conduct examinations for the grant of the requiredprofessional qualifications and to collaborate withrecongnized local and foreign professional andeducational Institutions to conduct courses inAccountancy which lead to exemptions from theInstitute\u2019s examinations;\n\n30\n\n35\n\n4The Institute of Certified Public Accountants(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(r) to prescribe the qualifications and disqualificationsapplicable for membership of the Institute and toestablish standards of professional conduct and ethicsfor members of the Institute;\n\n(s) to organize, supervise and regulate continuingprofessional education for the benefit of themembers;\n\n(t) to maintain library of both print and electronic media,books and periodicals, relating to Accountancy andrelated subjects for the use of members, students andthose interested in the field of Accountancy, Businessand Finance;\n\n(u) to grant scholarships, awards and prizes for those whoexcel in the field of Public Accountancy;\n\n(v) to award Diploma and Certificates to the members ofthe Institute and to those who fulfill the conditionsprescribed by the Institute;\n\n(w) to be a centre for accountancy development and topioneer the cause of the profession;\n\n(x) to develop partnership with all organizations thatshare our dedication to enhancing economic andsocial well being through inspiring leadership andexcellent management;\n\n(y) to identify and train accountants best equipped todeliver results in all sectors of industry, from largemultinationals to SMEs and from providers of publicservice to professional firms and non profitorganizations;30\n\nThe Institute of Certified Public Accountants(Incorporation)5\n\n(z) to stimulate interest in the importance of accountancyeducation as a tool to effective management;\n\n(aa) to enable accountants, whether members or otherwise,and directors and senior management of organizationsto communicate, meet and exchange information bysuch means as conferences, meetings, lectures,seminars and discussions;"
