    "chunk_text": "(2) The members who offer alms to the Dharmayathanayaannually shall be members with full membership rights.\n\n(3) Those who pay a sum of Rupees one thousand (Rs.1000.00) or more to the Corporation once, shall be its lifemembers.\n\nChairman Baddegama Pradeshiya Sabha, DivisionalSecretary, Baddegama, District Medical Officer Baddegama,Officer In-charge of Police Station Baddegama, GramaNiladhari Ganegama South are become member by theirdesignation.\n\n12.(1) The advisory board of this Corporation shallconsist of three High Priests well versed in and devoted tothe observance of Buddhist doctrine and two learned, elderlyand pious Buddhist laymen in addition to the Director ofDharmayathanaya and the Parivenadhipathi.\n\n30\n\nAdvisoryBoard.\n\nHow the sealof theCorporationis to beaffixed.\n\nHeadquartersof theCorporation.\n\nMembershipandmembershipfees.\n\nGanegama Sri Indasara DharmayathanaSanrakshana Sabhawa (Incorporation)5\n\n(2) Except the Director of Dharmayathanaya and theParivenadhipathi, all other members of the Advisory Boardreferred to above shall be elected at a general meeting by themajority vote of the members.\n\n13.(1) The first Director of the Corporation shall beReverend Pandith Keradewala Vajiragnana Thero (B.A.) theDirector of this Dharmayathanaya holding office at the timeof the coming into operation of this Act. The Director shallbe the Internal Administrator of the \u201cGanegama Sri IndasaraDharmayathana\u201d conducted by this Corporation and of anyother institutes, if any, to be established.\n\n(2) The office of the Director which will fall vacant afterthe present Director shall be filled by electing a Bhikku wellversed in and devoted to the observance of Buddhist doctrineand who belongs to this monastic sector."
