    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of June 10, 2016\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 13.06.2016)\n\nMEDICAL (AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the Medical Ordinance (Chapter 105)\n\nOrdered to be Published by the Minister of Health, Nutritionand Indigenous Medicine\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5.\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 43 of the Medical Ordinance (Chapter 105)(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of the section asamended is to incorporate consequential amendments to section 43 in compliance with theprovisions of new section 43A.\n\nClause 3 : This clause inserts new section 43A and 43B in the principal enactment andthe section makes provision for the provisional registration of dentists under the principalenactment and for the rights of persons provisionally registered as dentists.\n\n1Medical (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nShort title.\n\n25\n\n2\u2014PL 009970\u2014425 (05/2016)\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 64/2007.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE MEDICAL ORDINANCE(CHAPTER 105)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Medical (Amendment)Act, No. of 2016.\n\n2. Section 43 of the Medical Ordinance (Chapter 105)(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended as follows:\u2014\n\n(1)in subsection (1) thereof, by the substitution forthe words \u201cby a Degree Awarding Institute;\u201d of thewords and figures \u201cby a Degree Awarding Instituteand holds a certificate granted by the MedicalCouncil under subsection (3) of section 43A\u201d;\n\n(2)in subsection (1A) by the repeal of paragraph (c)thereof and the substitution therefor of the followingparagraphs:\u2014\n\n\u201c(c)has passed the special examinationprescribed in that behalf by the MedicalCouncil; and\n\n(d)holds a certificate granted by the MedicalCouncil under subsection (3) of section43A,\u201d;"
