    "chunk_text": "(ii)has passed the examinationnecessary for obtaining the Degreeof Bachelor of Dental Surgery ofthe University of Ceylon or acorresponding University or aDegree Awarding Institute, but has\n\n\u201cProvisionalregistrationof dentists.\n\nInsertion ofnew section43A and 43Bin theprincipalenactment.\n\n3Medical (Amendment)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(d)(i)holds a Degree of Bachelor ofDental Surgery or an equivalentqualification from any universityor dental school of any countryother than Sri Lanka, which isrecognized by the MedicalCouncil for the purposes of thissection having regard to thestandard of education in dentistryof such university or dentalschool; or\n\n(ii)has passed the examinationnecessary for obtaining the Degreeof Bachelor of Dental Surgery oran equivalent qualification fromany university or dental school ofany country other than Sri Lanka,which is recognized by theMedical Council for the purposesof this section, having regard tothe standard of education indentistry of such university ordental school but has not obtainedthat degree owing to the fact thathe has not completed the periodof internship required forobtaining that degree and the35\n\nMedical (Amendment)4\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nDirector-General of HealthServices has permitted him tocomplete the period of internshipin Sri Lanka; and\n\n(iii)has passed the special examinationprescribed in that behalf by theMedical Council.\n\n(2) The prescribed fee for provisionalregistration as a dentist shall be paid to theregistrar on application for registration.\n\n(3) (a) Where a person who is provisionallyregistered as a dentist applies to the MedicalCouncil for a certificate under this subsectionand the Medical Council is satisfied, onproduction of a certificate of internship and anevaluation certificate acceptable to theMedical Council, that he\u2014\n\n(i)has been engaged in employment forthe prescribed period in one or moreapproved hospitals or institutions;"
