    "chunk_size_bytes": 1892,
    "chunk_text": "(c)to use and support to sue drama and theatre andother arts to enable majority of society tounderstand and build self esteem, whileundrstanding tolerating, appreciating, admiringothers and their various ideologies, inclinations,behaviours, cultures that enable them tocommunicate and interact with each othereffectively and as a result support building a societyin which everybody can live in harmony and peace;\n\n(d)to support to create a society to understand thenature and build a good relationship with the naturethat enables living in harmony with nature;\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n30\n\n35\n\n3Janakaraliya Cultural Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n(f)to sponsor or and conduct workshops, conferences,seminars, group studies and public lectures ondrama and theatre in any part of the country oroutside Sri Lanka;\n\n(g)to grant assistance to individuals, primarycommunity organizations, governmentinstitutions for the achieving objectives of theFoundation.\n\n4.(1) The affairs of the Corporation shall, subject to theother provisions of this Act and the rules of the Corporation,made under Section 6, be administerd by a Board ofDirectors consisting of Chairman, Secretary, Treasurer andanother five members elected in accordance with such rules.\n\n(2) The first Board of the Corporation shall consist of themembers of the Board of Administration of the Foundationholding office on the day immediately preceding the date ofhis election.\n\n(3) A member of the Board of Directors shall unless hevacates his office earlier by death or resignation, holds officefor a period of four years reckoned from the date of hiselection.\n\n(4) If any member of the Board of Directors vacates hisoffice prior to the expiry of his term, his successor elected inaccordance with rules of the Corporation shall hold officeonly for the unexpired term of office of the member who hesucceeds."
