    "chunk_text": "(4) Any license, which has already beenissued under the principal enactment forfishing operations carried out by Trawl Nets inSri Lanka waters, shall not be renewed, and\n\nShort title.\n\nInsertion ofnew section28A to theprincipalenactment.\n\n\u201cProhibitionof TrawlingOperations.\n\nFisheries and Aquatic Resources (Amendment)2\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nProvided that, a license already issued for theuse of Trawl Nets and which is still in force onthe day preceding the date of commencementof this Act, shall notwithstanding this Act,continue to be valid for the purpose in respectof which the license has been issued, for theperiod specified in the license.\u201d.\n\n3.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 49(6) of the principal enactmentand shall have effect as section 49(7) of that enactment.\n\n49 (7). Any person who contravenes or failsto comply with the provisions of section 28Aof this Act shall commit an offence and shallon conviction after summary trial before aMagistrate be liable to an imprisonment for aterm not exceeding two years or to a fine notless than fifty thousand rupees.\u201d.\n\n4.Section 66 of the principal enactment is herebyamended by the insertion, immediately after the definitionof the expression \u201cSri Lanka Waters\u201d, of the following newdefinitions:\u2014\n\n\u201cTrawl Net\u201d means towing nets having a coneshaped body and a bag or cod end (madiya)connected to the apex with or without twowings connected to the other end.\n\n\u201cTrawling\u201d means any fishing operation carried outby dragging a Trawl Net mechanically alongthe bed or in mid water.\n\n5.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\n\u201cOffences.\n\nAmendmentof section 66of theprincipalenactment.\n\nInsertion ofnew section49(7) to theprincipalenactment.\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase of anyinconsistency.\n\n3Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (Amendment)"
