    "chunk_text": "THE GAZETTE OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPart II of January 01, 2016\n\nSUPPLEMENT\n\n(Issued on 04. 01. 2016)\n\nS. B. NAWINNA FOUNDATION (INCORPORATION)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto incorporate the S. B. Nawinna Foundation\n\nTo be presented in Parliament by Hon. Buddhika Pathirana, M. P. forMatara District\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\n(Private Member\u2019s Bill)\n\n1S. B. Nawinna Foundation(Incorporation)\n\n2\u2014PL 009703\u2014 225 (01/2016)\n\nPreamble.\n\nShort title.\n\nGeneralobjects of theCorporation.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAN ACT TO INCORPORATE THE S. B. NAWINNA FOUNDATION\n\nWHEREAS An Association called and known as\u201cS. B. Nawinna Foundation\u201d has heretofore been formed inthe purpose of effectually carrying out and transacting allobjects and matters connected with the said Foundationaccording to the rules agreed to by its members :\n\nAND WHEREAS the said Association has heretoforesuccessfully carried out and transacted the several objectsand matters for which it was formed and has applied to beincorporated and it will be for the public advantage to grantsuch application :\n\nBE it therefore enacted by the Parliament of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the S. B. NawinnaFoundation (Incorporation) Act, No. of 2016.\n\n2.From and after the date of commencement of this Act,such and so many persons as now are members of the \u201cS. B.Nawinna Foundation\u201d (hereinafter referred to as the\u201cFoundation\u201d) or shall hereafter be admitted members of theCorporation hereby constituted shall be a body corporate(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cCorporation\u201d) with perpetualsuccession under the name and style of \u201cS. B. NawinnaFoundation\u201d and by that name may sue and be sued in allcourts, with full power and authority to have and use aCommon Seal and alter the same at its pleasure."
