    "chunk_size_bytes": 2001,
    "chunk_text": "5.(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law the Corporation shall have the power to do allsuch acts and things as are necessary for or conducive orincidental to the carring out of the objects of the FoundationTrust.\n\n30\n\nGeneralPowers oftheCorporation.\n\n4The Seretse Khama Foundation Trust(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the powersconferred by subsection (1), the Corporation shall have thefollowing powers:\u2014\n\n(a)to acquire in any manner whatsoever and hold anyproperty movable or immovable which maybecomevested in it by any purchase, grant, gift, device orotherwise;\n\n(b)to sell, mortgage, lease, convey, devise, assign,exchnage or otherwise dispose of any suchproperty;\n\n(c)to invest found belonging to the Foundation Trustin Treasury Bonds, Treasury Bills and such otherSecurities as may be determined by the Corporation;\n\n(d)to open, operate, maintain and close bank accountsand to borrow or raise money with or withoutsecurity;\n\n(e)to engage, employ and dismiss officers and servantsrequired for the carrying out of the objects of theFoundation Trust;\n\n(f)to raise funds and receive grants, gifts or donationsin cash or kind;\n\n(g)to administer the officers of the Trust and manageits assets;\n\n(h)to engage in dialogue with Government and otherinstitutions and Banks in furtherance of the objectsof the Foundation Trust;\n\n(i)to determine what monies are to be consideredcapital and what income;\n\n(j)to derermin what expenses, costs and outgoings areproperly out of capital or income respectively;30\n\n5The Seretse Khama Foundation Trust(Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(k)to establish tourist resorts and provide touring andcab services, create new ventures within theobjectives of the Trust, lay out policies andeffectively implement them;\n\n(l)to purchase farms and agricultural properties; and\n\n(m)to do all such acts and things as are incidental orconducive for the carrying out of the objects of theFoundation Turst."
